Answer: Based on the search result, Russia's delivery of medical aid to the United States appears to have been a unilateral gesture rather than part of a disclosed reciprocal agreement. The article cites U.S. President Donald Trump confirming the receipt of aid, stating, "Russia sent us a very, very large planeload of things. Medical equipment, which was very nice," but does not mention any corresponding U.S. aid to Russia or a mutual pact; it notes only that both leaders "discussed closer cooperation" and agreed to work through the G20.

